| Algorithm            | Best Time | Average Time | Worst Time | Space Complexity                    |
| -------------------- | --------- | ------------ | ---------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Linear Search        | O(1)      | O(n)         | O(n)       | O(1)                                |
| Binary Search        | O(1)      | O(log n)     | O(log n)   | O(1) iterative / O(log n) recursive |
| Jump Search          | O(1)      | O(√n)        | O(√n)      | O(1)                                |
| Interpolation Search | O(1)      | O(log log n) | O(n)       | O(1)                                |
| Exponential Search   | O(1)      | O(log n)     | O(log n)   | O(1)                                |


| Algorithm      | Best Time  | Average Time            | Worst Time | Space Complexity |
| -------------- | ---------- | ----------------------- | ---------- | ---------------- |
| Bubble Sort    | O(n)       | O(n²)                   | O(n²)      | O(1)             |
| Selection Sort | O(n²)      | O(n²)                   | O(n²)      | O(1)             |
| Insertion Sort | O(n)       | O(n²)                   | O(n²)      | O(1)             |
| Merge Sort     | O(n log n) | O(n log n)              | O(n log n) | O(n)             |
| Quick Sort     | O(n log n) | O(n log n)              | O(n²)      | O(log n)         |
| Heap Sort      | O(n log n) | O(n log n)              | O(n log n) | O(1)             |
| Counting Sort  | O(n + k)   | O(n + k)                | O(n + k)   | O(k)             |
| Radix Sort     | O(nk)      | O(nk)                   | O(nk)      | O(n + k)         |
| Bucket Sort    | O(n + k)   | O(n + k)                | O(n²)      | O(n)             |
| Shell Sort     | O(n log n) | Depends on gap sequence | O(n²)      | O(1)             |


Notes
n = number of elements
k = range of input / number of buckets / digits
Binary Search requires a sorted array
Quick Sort is usually fastest in practice for arrays
Merge Sort is stable and good for linked lists
Heap Sort guarantees O(n log n) worst case
Counting/Radix/Bucket sorts are non-comparison sorts
